We are looking for a Senior Technical Sound Designer to join our digital game team at Wizards of the Coast. This role is anticipated to be a hybrid work position, with some work on-site and some work from home. The potential home studio for this role is Renton, WA.&nbsp;

What You’ll Do&nbsp;

• Design and develop features, tools, and workflows that align with the game’s creative vision and enhance production efficiency, in collaboration with the Audio Director and key stakeholders.&nbsp;

• Partner with cross-discipline technical experts to streamline processes, improve integration, and elevate overall product quality.&nbsp;

• Collaborate with game engineers to implement scalable and reliable audio pipelines that support production at all stages.&nbsp;

• Optimize audio assets and development workflows to meet the evolving technical and creative needs of the project.&nbsp;

• Identify and troubleshoot issues across disciplines, providing clear technical solutions and support to team members.&nbsp;

• Author and maintain documentation outlining workflows, standards, and best practices for consistency and knowledge sharing.&nbsp;

• Work closely with QA teams to investigate, escalate, and track audio-related bugs, ensuring timely resolution of critical issues.&nbsp;

• Proactively monitor and address performance and memory challenges, maintaining audio quality and player immersion without compromising efficiency.&nbsp;

• Create audio content when required, applying strong sound design skills and proficiency with both commercial and proprietary tools.&nbsp;

• Stay current with emerging audio technologies and innovations, translating them into technical direction and motivation for the audio team and project.&nbsp;

What You’ll Bring&nbsp;

• 5+ years of combined experience in the game industry as a Technical Sound Designer, deep familiar workflows as a Sound Designer, all contributing to high-quality game audio experiences.&nbsp;

• Proficient with AAA game engines, on the current pulse of emerging audio technology with a strong command of audio implementation and integration workflows/&nbsp;

• Advanced expertise in MetaSound and Wwise, including setup, optimization, and troubleshooting within complex game environments.&nbsp;

• Experience with Unreal Engine, Blueprint scripting, and engine tools that support&nbsp; large scale audio implementation and authoring.&nbsp;

• Proven experience designing and developing custom audio workflows and tools to enhance production efficiency.&nbsp;

• Highly collaborative, with a demonstrated ability to partner effectively across departments and foster a strong team dynamic.&nbsp;

• Comfortable with scripting and level design tools, and well-versed in end-to-end game development pipelines across disciplines.&nbsp;

